    <briefdescription>
<para>Marker interface for idempotent recovery operations. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Types implementing this interface guarantee that:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_idempotent_recovery_operation_1ac583e9dc96677d69ccaa779924a417e8" kindref="member">execute()</ref> with the same input produces the same output on retry</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>No side effects persist on repeated execution</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>State is not duplicated (e.g., no duplicate WAL entries)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Implementations are responsible for:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Unique request/operation IDs (e.g., transaction-id, operation-id)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Deduplication (checking if operation already completed)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Immutable recovery state (no conflicting concurrent modifications) </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
